d as owning the projected bytes. The 1962 reading was established on that edition's page images rather than its text layer, cross-read against the Benziger conformed printing. Differences from the antecedent: 1962 reads `Ecclesiae` where 1862 reads `Eccl6sise`; 1962 reads `Scripturis` where 1862 reads `Scriptfins`; 1962 reads `Hieronymum, Confessorem` where 1862 reads `Hier6nymum, Confess6rem`; 1962 reads `Doctorem` where 1862 reads `Doct6rem`; 1962 reads `providere` where 1862 reads `provid6re`; 1962 reads `praesta, quaesumus;` where 1862 reads `prasta, qwesumus;`; 1962 reads `suffragantibus meritis, quod` where 1862 reads `suffragdnjibus m6ritis, qiiod`; 1962 reads `opere docuit,` where 1862 reads `6pere d6cuit,`; 1962 reads `exercere` where 1862 reads `exerc6re`; 1962 reads `Dominum.` where 1862 reads `D6minum.`; 1862 sets no comma after the ut; 1862 prints the j-orthography (ejus, adjuvante); 1862 layer damage is heavy in this oration (Scriptfins, prasta, qwesumus, suffragdnjibus, qiiod) but every damaged word is recoverable letter by letter and each is clean in the 1962; nothing is inferred that the surrounding letters do not fix; 1862 conclusion is the short cue and so is the 1962's here. Corroboration: 1922 Mame carries 30 September (PDF p. 840); not transcribed, the 1862 settles the reading.","relationship":"editorial-projection-exact-to-target","source_date":"2026-09-03 project editorial projection; antecedent Pustet Ratisbon 1862","source_id":"passage.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-09-03.s-hieronymi-presbyteri-confessoris-ecclesiae-doctoris-collect","status":"collated","transformations":["join printed line wraps","remove stress accents","expand printed ae/oe ligatures to ae/oe","normalise consonantal i to the calendar's j orthography","apply the target printing's punctuation","carry the target's conclusion at its printed length"],"verification_locator":"printed p. 672, no. 3739, marked P; artifact PDF p. 753